  "question": {
    "text": "Which halogen is known to cause the reaction given below?",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "eP8fH",
      "text": "All halogens",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "UTSAA",
      "text": "&nbsp;Only Bromine",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Sbyue",
      "text": "Only Iodine",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "W2bdS",
      "text": "Only Chlorine",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>All <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;halides are known except the iodide. In this case, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> oxidises <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>&#8211;</mo></msup></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>.&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>Cu</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>However, many copper (I) compounds are unstable in aqueous solution and undergo disproportionation.&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mo>&#8594;</mo><mrow></mrow></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Cu</mi></math></p></blockquote>",
